  "solution": {
    "text": "Consider the following resonance structure<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/dadf9.JPG\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 182px;\" /><br /><br />The structures (2) and (3) show the partial single-bond character of the <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math> bonds, and (4) and (5) the partial double-bond character of the <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> bond. This explains the observed anomalies in the bond distances.",
